From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Benjamin Gregoire <Benjamin.Gregoire@inria.fr>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 17:22:53 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] The mode in the program semantics and the relational logic

sem_sopn (section EXEC_ASM) and the itree semantics (it_sems_core.v,
section WSW) take the SemMode in context: the whole program semantics
follows one instance, and the default one keeps every existing statement.
get_var_is, which reads the results of a call, stays partial: a result that
is not initialised is a failure of the call in both modes.

psem_core.v and psem_facts.v are generic in the mode where the two modes
agree (get_gvar_compat through Vm.getP_mode, the eq_on and use_mem lemmas,
sopn_toutP, the write_lval lemmas on the memory); sopn_tinP,
truncate_val_exec_sopn and exec_sopn_truncate_val stay in the partial mode,
where a success of exec_sopn says something about its arguments. The facts
the generic proofs were missing are added where they belong: Vm.getP_mode
and Vm.get_eq_mode (two variable maps equal on a variable in the partial
mode are equal on it in every mode) and, on the memory, write_mem_stable
and write_validw_eq in both modes.

relational_logic.v relates two programs under two modes: the section takes
{sm1 sm2 : SemMode}; the opn rules on eq require SameMode, the rules on
uincl require IsPartial (value_uincl is not monotone in the total mode),
two classes every existing proof infers by reflexivity. wequiv_asserts_left
is new. hoare_logic.v takes the mode in context, as the semantics it talks
about; psem.v needs nothing: with no mode in context its sections are the
partial ones.

Three proof scripts of the passes follow the new binders: two applications
of the opn rules discharge the class argument, and two explicit
applications take the mode as an argument. No statement of a pass changes.

The total mode never evaluates an expression to an undefined value
(sem_pexpr_defined, sem_pexprs_defined); use_mem_eassertP and
use_mem_eassertP_eq_on are the eassert counterparts of use_memP. The
comparison of the two modes the safety proof relies on is stated here too:
a defined variable reads the same in both modes (Vm.get_totalE), and in
the total mode an operator is its total semantics (sem_sop1_typed_total,
sem_sop2_typed_total).

(cherry picked from commit e6df4719f34dd3e4c462683ca3eda2fe13e24556)
